  <p><strong>Every article on MarketTriggers.com is meant to help a reader understand why U.S. markets move.</strong> This page explains how we choose topics, where our facts come from, how we fix mistakes, and how we keep content current.</p>

  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>We publish educational explainers about economic indicators, Federal Reserve policy, corporate events, sector dynamics, and market structure. We do not publish stock picks, price targets, trading signals, or personalized advice, and we do not accept payment to cover a company or security.</p>

  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We rely first on primary sources: the Bureau of Labor Statistics, the Bureau of Economic Analysis, the Census Bureau, the Federal Reserve, the U.S. Treasury, the SEC, and company filings.</li>
    <li>Every article lists the official sources it relies on, with links.</li>
    <li>We do not publish statistics, quotations, or data we cannot trace to a reliable source. When we describe a hypothetical scenario, we label it as one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Facts, analysis, and scenarios</h2>
  <p>We keep three kinds of statements apart: verifiable facts (what a report said), analysis (why it may matter), and scenarios (what could happen next). Market reactions described as typical are patterns investors have observed, not predictions.</p>

  <h2>How articles are produced</h2>
  <p>Our editors plan each article around a specific reader question, research it against the sources above, and review it before publication. We use software tools, including AI writing assistants, to help with research, outlining, and drafting. A human editor reviews every article for accuracy, checks facts against the cited sources, and is responsible for what is published.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>If we get something wrong, we fix it and note the correction at the end of the article with the date. Material corrections are never made silently. To report an error, email <a href="mailto:info.christopherkunz@gmail.com">info.christopherkunz@gmail.com</a> with the page URL and the statement in question.</p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>Economic data is revised and policy changes. We review evergreen explainers at least every six to twelve months and update them when the facts change. Each article shows its publication date and, after a substantial update, its last-updated date.</p>

  <h2>Independence and advertising</h2>
  <p>We may display advertising to support the site. Advertisers have no influence over what we cover or what we say, and ads are kept visually separate from editorial content. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how advertising cookies work.</p>

  <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
  <p>Our content is general education. It does not consider your personal situation and is not a recommendation to buy or sell anything. For decisions about your own money, consult a qualified, licensed professional.</p>

  <p>Questions about these standards? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a> or read <a href="/about/">about MarketTriggers.com</a>.</p>
